& [SharedLifecycleModule] is strict common behavior
  + [paths] are absolute, normalized, regular, non-reparse, and mutually distinct
  + [state] has an exact property set, canonical paths and timestamps, positive PID and sequence, and lowercase SHA-256 generation
  + [process_identity] is PID plus canonical executable plus exact UTC start time
  + [client] invokes the existing cantorctl with redirected bounded output and validates protocol, disposition, result kind, faults, and active binding
  + [state_write] is same-directory UTF-8 no-BOM temporary publication followed by atomic move

& [StartImplementation] is readiness before authority
  + [launch] is one hidden cantord with exactly --config and separate unique stdout and stderr logs
  + [readiness] is repeated authenticated cantorctl status within explicit bounds
  + [publication] occurs only after readiness and a second complete process-identity match
  + [duplicate] rejects a live matching state
  + [stale] requires explicit ReplaceStale after valid-state nonlive proof
  + [failure] stops only the exact process returned by that start attempt

& [HealthImplementation] is fresh
  + [precondition] is exact state and complete live process identity
  + [probe] is a fresh authenticated status through the state-bound client and configuration
  + [result] distinguishes start generation and sequence from current generation and sequence after refresh
  + [output] is strict machine JSON with process, service, uptime, logs, and checked time

& [StopImplementation] is graceful
  + [precondition] is exact state and complete live process identity
  + [binding] is a fresh authenticated status generation
  + [shutdown] is existing authenticated exact-generation service shutdown
  + [completion] is bounded confirmed process exit before exact state-file removal
  - never: force-kill, remove state on timeout, or signal a mismatched identity

& [AdversarialProof] is one real-binary lifecycle
  + [cases] is ready start, exact state and token exclusion, health, duplicate refusal, forged start-time health and stop refusal, unknown-state refusal, graceful stop, listener release, stale default refusal, explicit stale replacement, and failed-readiness cleanup
  + [binaries] are the Cargo-built production cantord and cantorctl targets
  + [result] is passed

& [NonclaimSet] is retained
  + [platform] is Windows PowerShell rather than cross-platform daemonization
  + [manager] is no Shaliach, Codex conversation, model-call, or autonomous recovery authority
  + [service] is no operating-system service installation or general supervisor
  + [semantics] is no new SOP interpretation, query, trust, package, or effect behavior
